                        <h2 class="blog_heading" id="list_1">1. When do you Need Plastic Surgery?</h2>
                        <p>People undergo plastic or cosmetic surgeries for two distinct reasons - one to correct medical conditions and the second to improve aesthetic features. You might need to undergo plastic surgery when:</p>
                        <ul class="disc_list">
                            <li>To correct genetic anomalies like birthmarks, webbed feet, etc.</li>
                            <li>To enhance and improve the shape of various body features, according to one’s needs</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>As for an ideal age, you should always wait until you are an adult to undergo any form of cosmetic surgery. Also, make sure that you prepare yourself mentally before undergoing plastic surgery. This is crucial, mainly because of the fact that these surgeries bring along a lot of changes that you need to be prepared for.</p>

                        <h2 class="blog_heading" id="list_2">2. Top 8 Life-Changing Benefits & Advantages Of Plastic Surgery</h2>
                        <p>Coming to the best advantages of plastic surgery, here are a few that you need to keep a check on the following ones.</p>
                        <ol style="margin-left: 30px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Boosts Self-Image and Self-Confidence</b><br>
                                One of the primary reasons people undergo plastic or cosmetic surgeries is to enhance physical features. When you look good, you feel better from within. If you are not satisfied with your appearance, chances are that undergoing plastic surgery can help with that dysphoria.<br>
                                Many people have reported feeling more confident with their bodies once they undergo a transformation. Witnessing their body look the way they have always dreamt it to is groundbreaking for some people to accept themselves and the way they look.
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Enhanced Physical Health</b><br>
                                There are several people who undergo plastic surgery to enhance their physical well-being. Just because someone is undergoing a rhinoplasty or a nose-reshaping surgery doesn’t always mean they are insecure about their nose shape and looks. It can very well mean that they need to undergo the procedure to improve their breathing and other issues related to their respiratory functions.<br>
                                Similarly, several women undergo breast reduction surgeries to further prevent the risks of misshaped and fibrocystic breasts. There are several plastic surgeries that are done to further enhance and improve the overall physical well-being of the patient. 
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Reconstructive Benefits for Genetic Anomalies</b><br>
                                There are several genetic conditions like cleft palate and webbed feet that affect one’s day-to-day lives and not to mention, that it affects one’s mental health as badly. In such cases, reconstructive surgery is the one way to enhance one’s physical features and prevent the impacts it brings to their life.<br>
                                Moreover, the benefits of plastic surgery extend as post-cancer treatments, especially in women with breast cancer. It is ideal for patients who have undergone a mastectomy to remove their cancerous breast/s. In such cases, plastic surgeries help develop a 3D areola and even augment breast shape and size, as per the patient’s needs.
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Minimally Invasive with Latest Medical Innovations</b><br>
                                One of the primary reasons people were iffy about plastic surgeries was because of the thought of extreme pain. However, with the consistent advancements in the medical field, the majority of plastic surgery procedures have now become minimally invasive.<br>
                                This has made the processes more favourable for the people who are planning on undergoing any plastic or cosmetic surgery procedures.
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Help with Weight Loss</b><br>
                                Another one of the pivotal advantages of plastic surgery is weight loss. It is ideal for patients who have been unable to shed off the excess pounds, even after months and years of trial and errors.<br>
                                Bariatric surgery procedures like liposuction and tummy tuck often help patients lose excess stored fats and pounds from their body. Plastic surgery is also beneficial in restoring a toned shape of the body after losing weight successfully.
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Long-term and Permanent Results</b><br>
                                If you want permanent changes to your physical looks and attributes, plastic surgery is the only way to go. These procedures provide results that are here to stay on your body permanently. So, it is likely that your investment in an ideal look is a one-time investment.<br>
                                However, you need to ensure that you stick to aftercare instructions after a plastic surgery procedure, especially when it comes to weight-loss related procedures like tummy tuck and liposuction. Make sure that you don’t go berserk with your lifestyle. Maintain a healthy diet and an active lifestyle to retain the results of the surgery.
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Improved Opportunities</b><br>
                                This is one of the benefits of plastic surgery that is very stereotypical when it comes to the standards of beauty in society. Many individuals who have undergone plastic surgeries have said that their changed looks generally enhance one’s chances of achieving more opportunities.<br>
                                It opens doors to several unattainable job roles and opportunities, including marketing, the fashion industry and even the beauty world.
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Easily Accessible</b><br>
                                Long gone are the days when plastic surgery was just a thing for the rich and popular people. With the advancing technologies and medical innovations, more and more people are getting easier access to these procedures and at very affordable costs too.<br>
                                Additionally, more and more <a href="https://www.iconiquebydrbkgarg.com/">plastic surgeon in gurgaon</a> is also getting into the field of aesthetic treatments and procedures, making this a more mainstream medical field now.
                            </li>
                        </ol>

                        <h2 class="blog_heading" id="takeaway">Take Away</h2>
                        <p>The benefits of plastic surgery are diverse and permanent. Not only does it help impact and improve the confidence of the people undergoing the procedure, but it also helps them lead a more comfortable and content life physically. However, it is essential that every patient makes informed decisions about any of the plastic surgery treatments and have realistic expectations out of the procedures.</p>
